'' fbc's astNewIIF converts a UDT arm into the string it EXTENDS -- zstring beside a
'' narrow character, wstring beside a wide one -- and refuses every other UDT arm.
'' tiko refused all of them, which cost AfxNova's DWSTRING ('TYPE DWSTRING EXTENDS
'' WSTRING') and tiko-editor's ProjectFolders_Normalize with TKO0655.
''
'' THE RUNTIME HALF IS THE POINT, and build/goldenrun.sh is what proves it: the first
'' accepted program SEGFAULTED. Each arm's own temporaries -- the DWS the then-arm
'' builds, and the string beside it -- were released after the JOIN, so taking the ELSE
'' arm ran a destructor over storage nothing had constructed. They are released inside
'' the arm now, where fbc puts them, and the source exercises BOTH arms for that reason.
''
'' The assertions below are substring tests and unordered (EXPECT-OUT is 'instr'), so
'' they say the arm blocks and a destructor exist, not where the destructor sits. What
'' would catch it moving back out is the runtime difference against fbc.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/iif-udt-extends-wstring.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0655
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: wiif.then
'' EXPECT-OUT: wiif.join
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN3DWSD1Ev
